🔢 Dry Run (Short Summary)

Input:

[3,1,5,8]

Modified:

[1,3,1,5,8,1]

DP builds from small intervals to large.

Final:

dp[0][5] = 167
⏱ Time Complexity

Triple loop:

O(n³)
📦 Space Complexity
O(n²)
🧠 Why Greedy Fails?

If you burst largest first,
you may lose future multiplication benefit.

Hence we reverse thinking:
Choose last balloon instead of first.

🎯 Interview Summary Answer

This is interval DP. Instead of choosing first balloon, choose which balloon bursts last in an interval. Use DP[left][right] to represent maximum coins for subproblem. Time complexity O(n³).

